        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0743" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94111/101: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName type="venue">U. S. S. “<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Potomac</hi>”</placeName>,] <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1937-11-30T23:55:00">November 30, 1937—11:55
                            p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 1—1:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0030. Think it best to send the neutrality proclamation for me to sign so that
                    there will be no delay.</p>
                <p>I take it that only the regular list of munitions will be based [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">barred?</hi>] from export but suggest immediate study of
                    other articles so that we can discuss advisability of enlarging list later on. I
                    think we should seek in every way possible to avoid helping one side and not the
                    other.</p>
                <p>Please advise what probable effect declaration of war will have on our Shanghai
                    and Tientsin position, also what is new from British angle.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin</hi> D. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
